# README Changelog

The root [`README.md`](../../README.md) has a **Changelog** section. Every time you create
a commit in this repository, add its entry there **in the same commit**.

## Rules

- **One row per commit**, inserted at the **top** of the table (newest first).
- Columns: `Date` (ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`), `Change` (one sentence, English, past tense, linking
  the documents touched), `Commit` (short SHA).
- The commit link is
  `https://github.com/ArnaudStorq/sundance-maintenance-validation/commit/<shortSha>`.
- **Skip pure housekeeping**: renames, folder moves, formatting or typo passes. Only log
  changes to what the documentation actually says.

## Procedure

A commit cannot contain its own SHA, and amending to insert it only produces a new SHA.
So **the Changelog trails one commit behind**: record commit *N* in commit *N+1*.

```powershell
git commit -m "Docs: <subject>"   # the documentation change
git log --oneline -1              # read its short SHA
# add the row for that SHA at the top of the README Changelog table, then:
git commit -am "Changelog: record <shortSha>"
git push
```

The `Changelog: record ...` commit is housekeeping, so it gets no row of its own — the
table never chases itself. Both commits can be pushed together.

## Example row

```markdown
| 2026-09-16 | Added [TeamCity jobs](ReferenceDocs/TeamCityJobs.md) — the nightly rule pass and the distributed HLOD generation, their parameters and their schedule | [`ee39f69`](https://github.com/ArnaudStorq/sundance-maintenance-validation/commit/ee39f69) |
```
